  "id": "jungian-typology",
  "term": "Jungian typology",
  "definition": "Jungian typology is a theory of psychological type that describes people in terms of attitudes of extraversion versus introversion and functions such as sensing, intuition, feeling, and thinking. In this framework, these tendencies are organized as opposing pairs, and a person is understood as relying more on one relatively dominant or “superior” type or function than its opposite.",
